  <!-- SECTION 1 -->
  <details class="sec" id="internships" open>
    <summary class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">01</span><h2>Summer 2027 Internships</h2></summary>
    <p class="sec-sub">Grouped by whether you can actually apply this year, not by geography. The ones you qualify for come first. Anything with a class-standing floor you do not clear yet sits at the bottom with the year to come back. Every card opens collapsed. Save the ones you want, hide the ones you do not.</p>

    <div class="note"><strong>Where this stands, 8 October 2026.</strong> <strong>LASP&rsquo;s Electrical Engineering Student Assistant closes Saturday 10 October</strong> and welcomes first-years. York Space Systems in Greenwood Village asks only that you have completed freshman year, and SpaceX and Stoke Space both name first-years in their pay tables. <strong>NIST SURF in Boulder opens mid-October</strong> and says first-years are &ldquo;encouraged to apply.&rdquo; Advanced Space moved down this week because its own page says &ldquo;at least a sophomore.&rdquo;<br><br>Everything here is an undergraduate internship and none require a degree in hand, only current enrollment. Where a listing needs class standing you do not have yet, it sits at the bottom of this section with the year it opens up, rather than being deleted.</div>

    <div class="jobbar">
      <p style="margin:0"><span class="counts" id="jb-counts">Save or hide as you read.</span> Your picks stay in this browser, so use the same one each time.</p>
      <div class="barbtns">
        <button class="btn" type="button" id="jb-toggle" aria-pressed="false">Show hidden</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" id="jb-list">Build my list to send Mom</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" id="jb-reset">Clear all picks</button>
      </div>
      <div class="pickbox" id="jb-box" hidden>
        <label for="jb-out">Copy this and text it to Mom. Next run keeps your saved ones and drops the hidden ones.</label>
        <textarea id="jb-out" readonly></textarea>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="geo">
      <h3>Apply now. You qualify</h3>
      <p>Open today, and the posting either names first-years or sets no class floor. Check the closing date on each.</p>
    </div>

    <article class="job" data-job="lasp">
      <details>
        <summary>
          <span class="job-t">Electrical Engineering Student Assistant</span>
          <span class="job-m">LASP, Laboratory for Atmospheric and Space Physics</span>
          <span class="job-l">CU Boulder east campus &middot; Boulder &middot; paid, during the school year</span>
          <span class="chip chip-now">Open, closes Saturday 10 October</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="job-body">
          <p>This is the one with a clock on it. LASP puts undergraduates on real NASA missions without leaving Boulder, and it is the line every company on this page wants to see. $20 to $26 an hour, 10 to 20 hours a week in term and 40 in summer.</p>
          <p class="elig"><strong>Eligibility, quoted.</strong> &ldquo;Enrolled full-time undergraduate student completing a BS/BA in Electrical Engineering or Engineering or other Applied Sciences,&rdquo; with &ldquo;Sophomore or Junior Standing&rdquo; listed as &ldquo;Preferred but not required.&rdquo; CU Boulder undergraduates only. Altium, soldering and oscilloscope experience is desired, which is you.</p>
          <p class="elig"><strong>Two things to ask before you apply.</strong> It lists a 3.0 GPA, and you may have no college GPA until fall grades post, so email LASP and ask how they count it. And it is &ldquo;a minimum of one year (two semesters and one summer),&rdquo; so decide that it is worth the semester before you start. Applications go through Handshake. The AI/FPGA posting closed 2 October and needed coursework you do not have yet.</p>
          <a class="go" href="https://lasp.colorado.edu/jobs/electrical-engineering-student-assistant/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the LASP posting &rsaquo;</a>
        </div>
      </details>
      <div class="job-acts">
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="save" aria-pressed="false">Save</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="hide" aria-pressed="false">Hide</button>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="job" data-job="york">
      <details>
        <summary>
          <span class="job-t">Automation Engineer Interns, Mission Operations and Space Vehicle</span>
          <span class="job-m">York Space Systems</span>
          <span class="job-l">Greenwood Village, Colorado &middot; Denver area</span>
          <span class="chip chip-now">Open, rolling, confirm it is current</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="job-body">
          <p>Two automation intern postings at a Colorado satellite maker, $22 to $26 an hour, 40 hours a week. Day-one work is automation and test scripting, so your Python counts.</p>
          <p class="elig"><strong>Eligibility, quoted.</strong> &ldquo;Enrollment in a 4-year degree program at an accredited university studying engineering. Must have completed at least Freshman year of the degree program.&rdquo; Applications are &ldquo;accepted on a rolling basis until the position is closed.&rdquo; &ldquo;Must have permanent authorization to work in the United States.&rdquo;</p>
          <p class="elig"><strong>The catch.</strong> The postings show no season or year, and the system dates their creation to about April 2025, but they are still listed today. Email York and ask whether these are for summer 2027 before you spend an evening. &ldquo;Completed at least Freshman year&rdquo; means after May 2027, which is exactly your summer.</p>
          <a class="go" href="https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d0821e1a6301823c22a8bd068b&amp;id=8a7887a896649c9c01967e1723c835dc&amp;source=&amp;lang=en" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the York posting &rsaquo;</a>
        </div>
      </details>
      <div class="job-acts">
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="save" aria-pressed="false">Save</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="hide" aria-pressed="false">Hide</button>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="job" data-job="stoke">
      <details>
        <summary>
          <span class="job-t">Summer 2027 Internship, Engineering</span>
          <span class="job-m">Stoke Space</span>
          <span class="job-l">Cape Canaveral FL, Kent WA, Moses Lake WA &middot; out of state</span>
          <span class="chip chip-now">Open, application window September to November</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="job-body">
          <p>A reusable-rocket company that names first-years in its pay table. 10 to 14 weeks starting May 2027.</p>
          <p class="elig"><strong>Eligibility, quoted.</strong> &ldquo;Pursuing Bachelor&rsquo;s or Master&rsquo;s degree in mechanical engineering, aerospace engineering, electrical engineering, computer engineering, computer science or a similar STEM field.&rdquo; Pay table: &ldquo;Freshman/Sophomore: $28.00/hour.&rdquo; They want &ldquo;hands-on engineering experience,&rdquo; which your drone, balloon and HUNCH work are. &ldquo;You may also be eligible for relocation support.&rdquo; No housing stated.</p>
          <p class="elig">Apply before the window closes in November.</p>
          <a class="go" href="https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/stokespacetechnologies/jobs/6175828004" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the Stoke posting &rsaquo;</a>
        </div>
      </details>
      <div class="job-acts">
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="save" aria-pressed="false">Save</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="hide" aria-pressed="false">Hide</button>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="job" data-job="spacex">
      <details>
        <summary>
          <span class="job-t">Summer 2027 Engineering Internship and Co-op</span>
          <span class="job-m">SpaceX</span>
          <span class="job-l">Hawthorne CA, Starbase TX, Redmond WA, Bastrop TX and other sites &middot; out of state</span>
          <span class="chip chip-now">Open, rolling, but they lean upperclassmen</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="job-body">
          <p>Re-read 8 October 2026 on their board: first posted 3 August, updated 29 September, no closing date. Their pay table has a first-year line, which is the best sign on this page that they take them.</p>
          <p class="elig"><strong>Eligibility, quoted.</strong> &ldquo;Must be enrolled in a bachelor&rsquo;s degree program in an engineering, physics or math discipline by the start of employment,&rdquo; plus &ldquo;3+ months of applied engineering experience (internship, laboratory, and personal/team project experience is applicable).&rdquo; Pay: &ldquo;Engineering Intern/Freshman/Sophomore: $28.00/hour.&rdquo; A 3.5 GPA is preferred. At least 12 consecutive weeks starting May or June 2027. Relocation is a possible stipend, no housing stated.</p>
          <p class="elig"><strong>The honest gap.</strong> Their own FAQ says the program is predominantly upperclassmen and graduate students and favors hands-on project history. Your Arvada internship and HUNCH lead are that history. Apply anyway, and apply again next year.</p>
          <a class="go" href="https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/spacex/jobs/8621740002" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the SpaceX posting &rsaquo;</a>
        </div>
      </details>
      <div class="job-acts">
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="save" aria-pressed="false">Save</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="hide" aria-pressed="false">Hide</button>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="job" data-job="nasa">
      <details>
        <summary>
          <span class="job-t">OSTEM internships, summer 2027</span>
          <span class="job-m">NASA Office of STEM Engagement</span>
          <span class="job-l">Centers nationwide &middot; out of state</span>
          <span class="chip chip-soon">Summer 2027 closes 1 March 2027, opening date not published</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="job-body">
          <p>NASA&rsquo;s own internship program, paid, across centers. The page gives no opening date for any session, so check it monthly.</p>
          <p class="elig"><strong>Eligibility, quoted.</strong> &ldquo;Be a full-time or part-time college student (undergraduate through graduate-level).&rdquo; 18 or older by session start, 3.0 GPA. The page never says &ldquo;freshman&rdquo; and sets no class floor. Stipend is &ldquo;based on academic level and session duration,&rdquo; no amount given. &ldquo;Interns are responsible for making their own housing arrangements.&rdquo; The Pathways track wants 15 completed semester hours, which you would have after this fall.</p>
          <a class="go" href="https://www.nasa.gov/learning-resources/internship-programs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the NASA internship page &rsaquo;</a>
        </div>
      </details>
      <div class="job-acts">
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="save" aria-pressed="false">Save</button>
        <button class="btn" type="button" data-act="hide" aria-pressed="false">Hide</button>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="job" data-job="bae-national">
      <details>
        <summary>
          <span class="job-t">Mechanical Engineering Intern, Summer 2027 (Hybrid)</span>
          <span class="job-m">BAE Systems, Electronic Systems</span>
          <span class="job-l">Nashua, New Hampshire &middot; out of state</span>
          <span class="chip chip-now">Open, no fixed deadline</span>
