    </a>

    <a class="card" href="https://www.colorado.edu/center/spacegrant/cu-student-space-grant-positions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      <div class="card-top"><p class="role">&#9733; Colorado Space Grant Consortium, paid student research</p><span class="pay event">Paid stipend</span></div>
      <p class="org">NASA-funded, Discovery Learning Center, CU Boulder campus</p>
      <p class="loc">Verified 25 Sept &middot; eligibility: open to all CU Boulder students, all majors, all years, <strong>no citizenship restriction</strong></p>
      <p class="why">NASA money that pays CU undergraduates to build and fly real hardware, and it is on your campus. Their WARP-SPEED programme is built specifically for students in their early semesters: skill-building workshops, then a project team in robotics, wearable tech, environmental monitoring or high-altitude balloon experiments, running through spring 2027. <strong>Status, 25 September:</strong> this year&rsquo;s WARP-SPEED closed on 2 September, the Fall 2026 hourly application form reads &ldquo;currently closed,&rdquo; and paid research team positions read &ldquo;None at this time.&rdquo; Their volunteer route is open: a NASA Challenge team interest form, and a form to propose your own project. Their own answer to missing it is &ldquo;we encourage students who wish to participate to apply as many times as it takes.&rdquo; Watch this page and take the next opening.</p>
