    <div class="note"><strong>Not yet, but get ready.</strong> These are real and worth knowing, and you are not eligible today.<br><br>
    <strong>AIAA Foundation undergraduate scholarships</strong>, up to about $2,500, roughly thirty a year. Their window is 15 October to 31 January, but their programme description says it &ldquo;offers scholarships to college sophomores, juniors, and seniors,&rdquo; and eligibility also requires a current AIAA student membership, at least one completed semester of full-time college, and a cumulative GPA of 3.300. Your first eligible cycle is the one that opens <strong>15 October 2027</strong>. Join the CU AIAA student chapter this fall so the membership clock is already running. <a class="inline" href="https://aiaa.org/get-involved/university-students/undergraduate-scholarships-graduate-awards/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#7fa6ff;text-decoration:none;">AIAA scholarships page</a><br><br>
    <strong>AMA Foundation scholarships</strong>, up to $15,000 across several awards for students in engineering and technical degrees. The catch is on their own eligibility list: &ldquo;A current AMA membership, in addition to having been an AMA member for 36 out of the past 48 months prior to that year&rsquo;s application deadline.&rdquo; That is a three-year membership history, so joining an AMA club now (see the drone section) starts a clock that pays out in your senior year. Their application portal currently shows grants only, no open scholarship applications. <a class="inline" href="https://amafoundation.modelaircraft.org/scholarships" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#7fa6ff;text-decoration:none;">AMA Foundation scholarships</a><br><br>
    <strong>Colorado Space Business Roundtable fellowship</strong>, a paid Colorado aerospace fellowship with Lockheed, Boeing, ULA, BAE and Sierra Space among the host companies. Their page still describes the June 2026 programme, so the 2027 cycle has not been posted. Check it in the spring. <a class="inline" href="https://coloradosbr.org/fellowship/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#7fa6ff;text-decoration:none;">CSBR fellowship page</a><br><br>
    <strong>Astronaut Scholarship Foundation</strong> and the <strong>Matthew Isakowitz Fellowship</strong> both require junior or senior standing, so they are a 2029 conversation, not a 2026 one.</div>

    <div class="note"><strong>Removed this run, so you do not waste an evening.</strong> The <strong>Lockheed Martin STEM Scholarship</strong> came off the page: the old link 404s, and Lockheed&rsquo;s working page now says &ldquo;Lockheed Martin will not be offering new STEM scholarships&rdquo; while they rework the programme. The <strong>AUVSI Foundation</strong> came off too: its link 404s, the foundation&rsquo;s current domain fails its own security certificate, and its most recent cycle closed on 31 July 2026.</div>
